WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Open an iron hand-warmer,
and it gets hot.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.610
In this cup, citric acid
meets bicarbonate of soda,

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.810
and the mixture goes cold.

4
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.090
Two reactions.

5
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.250
One warms up.

6
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.690
One cools down.

7
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.890
So where does the energy go?

8
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.250
Does the hand-warmer make new energy?

9
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.430
Does the cold cup destroy some?

10
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.030
In this mission, you'll meet
exothermic and endothermic

11
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.590
reactions, and tell them
apart with a thermometer.

12
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.910
You'll find out why melting
ice is not a reaction.

13
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.050
And you'll ask: if a candle
needs a match to start,

14
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.150
is it taking energy in?

15
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.530
Your mission: explain where
the energy goes when a reaction

16
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.580
gets hot or cold.
